Dialogue: 3,0:00:01.25,0:00:07.00,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}BURNSIDE'S BRIDGE · ANTIETAM, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.25,0:00:31.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}So imagine you are one of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.94,0:00:33.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A Union infantryman.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.02,0:00:34.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}You are nineteen, or thirty-five.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.81,0:00:36.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}You have been marching for days.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:30.50,0:00:36.25,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1038 0 l 1038 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:00:30.50,0:00:36.25,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:00:30.50,0:00:36.25,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:00:30.50,0:00:36.25,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A NEW YORK REGIMENT · ANTIETAM CAMPAIGN, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.51,0:00:53.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}But something is about to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.58,0:00:56.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A 37-year-old army doctor has spent the summer
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.46,0:00:59.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}building a system to get men like you off the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.72,0:01:01.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Antietam is one of its first tests.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:51.76,0:00:57.51,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1317 0 l 1317 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:00:51.76,0:00:57.51,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:00:51.76,0:00:57.51,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:00:51.76,0:00:57.51,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}DR. JONATHAN LETTERMAN (SEATED) WITH HIS STAFF · NOV. 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.36,0:01:05.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}This is what it was like to be wounded in the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.03,0:01:06.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}American Civil War.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.15,0:01:09.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}From the moment the bullet hit, to the saw, to the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.11,0:01:10.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}hospital, to the long road home.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.00,0:01:13.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}From the Army's own records, and the words of the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.90,0:01:14.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}men who lived it.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:02.61,0:01:08.36,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1338 0 l 1338 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:01:02.61,0:01:08.36,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
