Dialogue: 3,0:03:00.59,0:03:06.34,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE POTOMAC CROSSING · AFTER ANTIETAM, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.33,0:03:27.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A private in the 135th Pennsylvania, shot by
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.47,0:03:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}accident the day after the battle, wrote home from a
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.17,0:03:32.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}hospital near the field.
Dialogue: 2,0:03:24.58,0:03:30.33,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:03:24.58,0:03:30.33,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:03:24.58,0:03:30.33,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:03:24.58,0:03:30.33,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE LUTHERAN CHURCH · SHARPSBURG, MD., 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.30,0:03:41.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}He died less than three weeks after he was hit.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.06,0:03:44.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And for every wounded man, the next question was simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.35,0:03:45.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Would anyone come for you?
Dialogue: 2,0:03:38.55,0:03:44.30,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
