Dialogue: 3,0:04:52.00,0:04:57.75,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}UNION CAMP AT CUMBERLAND LANDING · PENINSULA CAMPAIGN, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.37,0:05:15.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Then came the end of August, and the second battle
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.02,0:05:15.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}at Bull Run.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:12.62,0:05:16.05,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:12.62,0:05:16.05,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:12.62,0:05:16.05,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:05:12.62,0:05:16.05,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}WAGON TEAMS IN BIVOUAC · VIRGINIA, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.70,0:05:27.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In Washington, 250 ambulances were scraped together
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.27,0:05:28.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}in a single afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.81,0:05:29.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Most were new.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.78,0:05:32.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The horses had never been harnessed.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:23.95,0:05:29.70,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:23.95,0:05:29.70,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:23.95,0:05:29.70,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:05:23.95,0:05:29.70,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMBULANCE REPAIR SHOP · WASHINGTON, D.C.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.75,0:05:34.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The drivers were hired in a hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.71,0:05:37.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A report later printed in the Official Records
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.35,0:05:38.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}conceded what happened next.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:33.00,0:05:38.75,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:33.00,0:05:38.75,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:33.00,0:05:38.75,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:05:33.00,0:05:38.75,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMBULANCES AND SUPPLY WAGONS PARKED · 1864
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.39,0:05:56.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Picture it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.08,0:05:58.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A late-summer field in Virginia. No shade.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.74,0:06:00.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}No water unless someone brings it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.89,0:06:02.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And you cannot stand.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:55.64,0:06:01.39,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:55.64,0:06:01.39,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:55.64,0:06:01.39,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:05:55.64,0:06:01.39,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FARMHOUSE HOSPITAL · FAIR OAKS, VA., 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.52,0:06:15.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A volunteer from Massachusetts went to that field
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.56,0:06:17.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}with wagons of supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.04,0:06:18.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Her name was Clara Barton.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.65,0:06:20.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}We will meet her again.
Dialogue: 2,0:06:12.77,0:06:18.52,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1188 0 l 1188 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:12.77,0:06:18.52,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:12.77,0:06:18.52,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:06:12.77,0:06:18.52,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}CLARA BARTON · PHOTOGRAPHED BY MATHEW BRADY'S STUDIO
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.52,0:06:23.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}There was one bright spot in that disaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.14,0:06:25.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A few ambulances from the Army of the Potomac,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.93,0:06:29.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}already run under a new set of rules, had been sent
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.03,0:06:30.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}to help at Pope's battles.
Dialogue: 2,0:06:20.77,0:06:26.52,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1081 0 l 1081 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:20.77,0:06:26.52,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:20.77,0:06:26.52,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:06:20.77,0:06:26.52,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMBULANCES PARKED · WASHINGTON, D.C., JULY 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.55,0:06:41.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Something had to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.09,0:06:44.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And one man in the Army of the Potomac had already
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.29,0:06:44.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}started.
Dialogue: 2,0:06:39.80,0:06:45.20,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1124 0 l 1124 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:39.80,0:06:45.20,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:39.80,0:06:45.20,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:06:39.80,0:06:45.20,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}DR. JONATHAN LETTERMAN WITH HIS STAFF · NOV. 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.42,0:07:05.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}He had been chosen by a reforming new Surgeon
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.32,0:07:08.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}General, William Hammond, who wanted a modern army
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.54,0:07:09.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}medical service.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:02.67,0:07:08.42,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:02.67,0:07:08.42,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:02.67,0:07:08.42,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:07:02.67,0:07:08.42,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SURGEONS AND HOSPITAL STEWARDS IN WASHINGTON
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.02,0:07:13.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Letterman found an army worn out by disease and by
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.02,0:07:14.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the Peninsula fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.39,0:07:17.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}He began with the problem that had failed the
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.09,0:07:18.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}wounded again and again:
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.53,0:07:20.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}getting them off the field.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:10.27,0:07:16.02,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:10.27,0:07:16.02,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:10.27,0:07:16.02,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:07:10.27,0:07:16.02,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}UNION CAMP · PENINSULA CAMPAIGN, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.68,0:07:52.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The light two-horse wagons brought men in from the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.85,0:07:55.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The heavier four-horse wagons carried men who had
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.57,0:07:57.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}already been treated further to the rear.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.85,0:07:59.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Each job had its own vehicle.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:49.93,0:07:55.68,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1188 0 l 1188 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:49.93,0:07:55.68,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:49.93,0:07:55.68,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ENGRAVING · MEDICAL AND SURGICAL HISTORY OF THE WAR (1883)
Dialogue: 3,0:07:49.93,0:07:55.68,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A TWO-HORSE AMBULANCE (ROSECRANS / WHEELING PATTERN)
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.91,0:08:03.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}These were soldiers, permanently detailed from the ranks.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.59,0:08:05.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Not teamsters. Not bandsmen.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.40,0:08:07.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Not frightened civilians.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:00.16,0:08:05.91,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1210 0 l 1210 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:00.16,0:08:05.91,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:00.16,0:08:05.91,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:08:00.16,0:08:05.91,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMBULANCE CORPS, 57TH NEW YORK · PLACE NOT IDENTIFIED
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.76,0:08:26.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Before, healthy men had left the firing line to help
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.88,0:08:30.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}a wounded friend to the rear, and often did not come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.35,0:08:33.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now the fighting men kept fighting, and trained men
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.40,0:08:34.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}did the carrying.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:24.01,0:08:29.76,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:24.01,0:08:29.76,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:24.01,0:08:29.76,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:08:24.01,0:08:29.76,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}STRETCHER DRILL · ARMY OF THE POTOMAC, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.86,0:08:36.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They drilled like infantry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.45,0:08:38.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Letterman's orders went down to the feet:
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.86,0:08:41.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the front man steps off with the left foot, the rear
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.91,0:08:44.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}man with the right, so the stretcher would not sway.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:35.11,0:08:40.86,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1167 0 l 1167 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:35.11,0:08:40.86,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:35.11,0:08:40.86,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:08:35.11,0:08:40.86,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMBULANCE DRILL IN THE FIELD · AFTER ANTIETAM, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.41,0:08:48.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Water kegs were rinsed and filled every day, so an
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.31,0:08:50.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}ambulance could move at any moment.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:45.66,0:08:50.75,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:45.66,0:08:50.75,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:45.66,0:08:50.75,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:08:45.66,0:08:50.75,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMBULANCE CORPS DRILL · PLACE NOT IDENTIFIED
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.83,0:09:32.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}From October, medicines would be issued by brigade,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.01,0:09:35.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}and handed to the regiments as needed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.37,0:09:38.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A regiment's chest of medicine could no longer
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.23,0:09:39.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}simply vanish on the road.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:30.08,0:09:35.83,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 998 0 l 998 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:30.08,0:09:35.83,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:30.08,0:09:35.83,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ENGRAVING · MEDICAL AND SURGICAL HISTORY OF THE WAR (1883)
Dialogue: 3,0:09:30.08,0:09:35.83,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A MEDICINE WAGON (PEROT PATTERN)
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.30,0:09:42.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And the vehicles themselves improved.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.61,0:09:45.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The best of the later war was the Rucker wagon:
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.54,0:09:48.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}four wheels, springs, about 1,100 pounds, with a
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.53,0:09:51.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}water cask under the driver's seat and stretchers
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.58,0:09:53.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}that folded into seats.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:40.55,0:09:46.30,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 998 0 l 998 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:40.55,0:09:46.30,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:40.55,0:09:46.30,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ENGRAVING · MEDICAL AND SURGICAL HISTORY OF THE WAR (1883)
Dialogue: 3,0:09:40.55,0:09:46.30,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE RUCKER AMBULANCE WAGON
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.47,0:09:55.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The Army's own history called it the most
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.78,0:09:59.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}serviceable ambulance wagon of the latter part of the war.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:53.72,0:09:59.46,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 998 0 l 998 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:53.72,0:09:59.46,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:53.72,0:09:59.46,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ENGRAVING · MEDICAL AND SURGICAL HISTORY OF THE WAR (1883)
Dialogue: 3,0:09:53.72,0:09:59.46,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE RUCKER AMBULANCE WAGON
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.51,0:10:02.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}So for now, it would exist only in the Army of the
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.35,0:10:02.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Potomac.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.81,0:10:05.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And it was barely five weeks old when Robert E.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.48,0:10:07.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Lee's army crossed into Maryland.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:59.76,0:10:05.51,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:59.76,0:10:05.51,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:59.76,0:10:05.51,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:09:59.76,0:10:05.51,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PONTOON BRIDGE AT BERLIN, MD. · OCT. 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.27,0:10:12.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The line of battle ran six to seven miles.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.70,0:10:15.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Letterman wrote that the hospitals were therefore
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.53,0:10:16.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}very numerous.
Dialogue: 2,0:10:10.52,0:10:16.27,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:10.52,0:10:16.27,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:10.52,0:10:16.27,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:10:10.52,0:10:16.27,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}UNION ARTILLERY · ANTIETAM, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.79,0:10:18.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Letterman was on the field that day.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.93,0:10:21.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}No one engaged on that hotly contested field, he
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.78,0:10:24.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}wrote, can ever forget the intense interest with
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.63,0:10:27.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}which he watched the progress of that battle.
Dialogue: 2,0:10:17.04,0:10:22.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:17.04,0:10:22.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:17.04,0:10:22.79,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:10:17.04,0:10:22.79,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A FIELD CAMP AFTER ANTIETAM, OCT. 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.80,0:10:45.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Every one of those men who was still alive needed to
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.72,0:10:47.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}be found, carried, sorted and treated.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.85,0:10:50.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}By an ambulance corps barely six weeks old.
Dialogue: 2,0:10:43.05,0:10:48.80,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1167 0 l 1167 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:43.05,0:10:48.80,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:43.05,0:10:48.80,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:10:43.05,0:10:48.80,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMBULANCE DRILL · THE NEW CORPS SOON AFTER ANTIETAM
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.31,0:11:03.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}He chose barns over houses.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.94,0:11:06.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Barns well provided with hay and straw, he wrote,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.89,0:11:08.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}were better ventilated.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.27,0:11:11.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Where he could, he laid the wounded in the open air
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.34,0:11:12.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}beside them.
Dialogue: 2,0:11:02.56,0:11:08.31,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1360 0 l 1360 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:02.56,0:11:08.31,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:02.56,0:11:08.31,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:11:02.56,0:11:08.31,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FIELD HOSPITAL AT SMITH'S FARM, KEEDYSVILLE · AFTER ANTIETAM
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.51,0:11:15.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Even so, he admitted, the hospitals were not always
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.62,0:11:17.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}beyond the reach of the enemy's guns.
Dialogue: 2,0:11:12.76,0:11:18.27,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:12.76,0:11:18.27,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:12.76,0:11:18.27,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:11:12.76,0:11:18.27,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FARMHOUSE ON THE ANTIETAM FIELD, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.42,0:11:32.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}General Joseph Hooker, wounded in the foot, was
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.11,0:11:33.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}treated at the Pry house.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.53,0:11:36.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The Park Service notes the wound had filled his boot.
Dialogue: 2,0:11:29.67,0:11:35.42,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:29.67,0:11:35.42,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:29.67,0:11:35.42,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:11:29.67,0:11:35.42,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE SHERRICK FARM · ANTIETAM, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.01,0:11:40.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}At the Roulette farm, which lay in the path of the
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.02,0:11:43.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Union advance on the Sunken Road, the barn became a
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.09,0:11:44.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}field hospital for the wounded.
Dialogue: 2,0:11:37.26,0:11:43.01,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1274 0 l 1274 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:37.26,0:11:43.01,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:37.26,0:11:43.01,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:11:37.26,0:11:43.01,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE MUMMA FARM, NEIGHBOR OF THE ROULETTE FARM · ANTIETAM
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.41,0:11:48.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Into one of those field hospitals came Clara Barton,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.47,0:11:51.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}with a wagon of supplies she had brought herself.
Dialogue: 2,0:11:45.66,0:11:51.41,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:45.66,0:11:51.41,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:45.66,0:11:51.41,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:11:45.66,0:11:51.41,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}CLARA BARTON
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.81,0:12:24.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And he wrote what he saw.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.52,0:12:27.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The poor wounded, mutilated soldiers that yet have
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.95,0:12:31.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}life and sensation, make a most horrid picture.
Dialogue: 2,0:12:23.06,0:12:28.81,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:12:23.06,0:12:28.81,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:12:23.06,0:12:28.81,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:12:23.06,0:12:28.81,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SHARPSBURG, MD. · 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.63,0:12:34.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A New York soldier remembered comrades with wounds
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.86,0:12:37.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}of all conceivable shapes, brought in and placed
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.97,0:12:38.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}side by side.
Dialogue: 2,0:12:31.88,0:12:37.63,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:12:31.88,0:12:37.63,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:12:31.88,0:12:37.63,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:12:31.88,0:12:37.63,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A ROAD IN SHARPSBURG, MD. · 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.58,0:13:03.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}But compared with Second Bull Run, three weeks
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.09,0:13:04.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}earlier, it was a different war.
Dialogue: 2,0:13:00.83,0:13:05.23,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:13:00.83,0:13:05.23,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:13:00.83,0:13:05.23,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:13:00.83,0:13:05.23,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}BURNSIDE'S BRIDGE · ANTIETAM, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.11,0:13:20.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}At a farm hospital, one blinded Confederate soldier
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.70,0:13:21.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}was heard to say:
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.89,0:13:25.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}some darned Yank has shot away my eyes, but I feel
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.41,0:13:27.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}as strong otherwise as ever.
Dialogue: 2,0:13:17.36,0:13:23.11,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:13:17.36,0:13:23.11,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:13:17.36,0:13:23.11,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:13:17.36,0:13:23.11,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FARMHOUSE ON THE ANTIETAM FIELD, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.62,0:14:14.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Families arrived to take their badly wounded sons home.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.78,0:14:17.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Letterman thought the journey often killed them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.54,0:14:20.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It was impossible, he wrote, to convince them.
Dialogue: 2,0:14:11.87,0:14:17.62,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:14:11.87,0:14:17.62,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:14:11.87,0:14:17.62,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:14:11.87,0:14:17.62,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A FIELD CAMP AFTER ANTIETAM, OCT. 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.05,0:14:50.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In doubtful cases, the three would consult together,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.17,0:14:53.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}and a majority would decide whether to operate and how.
Dialogue: 2,0:14:47.30,0:14:53.05,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:14:47.30,0:14:53.05,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:14:47.30,0:14:53.05,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:14:47.30,0:14:53.05,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SURGEONS OF THE NINTH CORPS · 1864
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.93,0:14:56.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}One assistant was to give the anaesthetic.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.22,0:14:59.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Others would dress wounds, keep records, and feed the men.
Dialogue: 2,0:14:54.18,0:14:59.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1338 0 l 1338 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:14:54.18,0:14:59.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:14:54.18,0:14:59.79,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:14:54.18,0:14:59.79,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A SURGEON AND OFFICER AT A TENT · ARMY OF THE POTOMAC, 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.14,0:15:10.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now the chain was complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.90,0:15:14.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Just behind each regiment, a medical officer set up
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.21,0:15:16.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}a small depot for first aid.
Dialogue: 2,0:15:09.39,0:15:15.14,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1531 0 l 1531 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:15:09.39,0:15:15.14,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:15:09.39,0:15:15.14,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:15:09.39,0:15:15.14,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A CONFEDERATE FIRING-LINE HOSPITAL CAMP, CAPTURED · PETERSBURG, 1864
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.36,0:15:43.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Letterman never used the word triage.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.39,0:15:45.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}But historians see its roots here.
Dialogue: 2,0:15:41.61,0:15:45.65,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:15:41.61,0:15:45.65,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:15:41.61,0:15:45.65,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:15:41.61,0:15:45.65,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FIELD HOSPITAL TENTS · BRANDY STATION, VA.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.70,0:15:49.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The first great test of the full system came at
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.08,0:15:51.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Fredericksburg, in December 1862.
Dialogue: 2,0:15:45.95,0:15:51.70,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1553 0 l 1553 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:15:45.95,0:15:51.70,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:15:45.95,0:15:51.70,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:15:45.95,0:15:51.70,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMBULANCES AT MARYE'S HEIGHTS, FREDERICKSBURG (DATE AS PRINTED: 1864)
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.62,0:16:25.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}So here is where you are now, if you were hit in
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.82,0:16:26.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}that winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.62,0:16:28.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Carried by men in green bands.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.62,0:16:31.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Sorted by a surgeon chosen for his skill.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.35,0:16:34.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Laid on a table in a division hospital, often within
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.81,0:16:35.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}hours.
Dialogue: 2,0:16:22.87,0:16:28.62,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1017 0 l 1017 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:16:22.87,0:16:28.62,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:16:22.87,0:16:28.62,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ENGRAVING · HARPER'S WEEKLY, 1865
Dialogue: 3,0:16:22.87,0:16:28.62,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}INSIDE A HOSPITAL TENT · PETERSBURG, 1864–65
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.66,0:16:38.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In Washington, a few days later, a new volunteer
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.37,0:16:40.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}nurse heard the shout through her hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.80,0:16:42.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They've come, they've come.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.33,0:16:44.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Hurry up, ladies, you're wanted.
Dialogue: 2,0:16:35.91,0:16:41.66,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:16:35.91,0:16:41.66,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:16:35.91,0:16:41.66,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:16:35.91,0:16:41.66,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}LOUISA MAY ALCOTT
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.58,0:16:46.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Her name was Louisa May Alcott.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.39,0:16:48.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The Fredericksburg wounded had arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.67,0:16:51.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And for many of them, what came next was the
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.24,0:16:52.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}operating table.
Dialogue: 2,0:16:44.83,0:16:50.58,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:16:44.83,0:16:50.58,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:16:44.83,0:16:50.58,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:16:44.83,0:16:50.58,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}LOUISA MAY ALCOTT · AS A NURSE, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.69,0:17:07.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}So now you are on the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.44,0:17:10.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Picture a door laid across two barrels, or a plank
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.56,0:17:13.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}in a barn, under whatever light there is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.11,0:17:15.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A surgeon in a stained coat looks down at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.98,0:17:17.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}What happens next?
Dialogue: 2,0:17:05.94,0:17:11.69,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:17:05.94,0:17:11.69,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:17:05.94,0:17:11.69,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:17:05.94,0:17:11.69,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A HOUSE USED AS A HOSPITAL · NEW BERNE, N.C.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.55,0:17:20.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}You have probably heard that Civil War soldiers bit
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.53,0:17:23.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}on a bullet while the surgeon worked, wide awake.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.38,0:17:26.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}For the Union army, the records say otherwise.
Dialogue: 2,0:17:17.80,0:17:23.55,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1210 0 l 1210 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:17:17.80,0:17:23.55,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:17:17.80,0:17:23.55,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:17:17.80,0:17:23.55,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}MEDICAL DIRECTORS, ARMY OF THE CUMBERLAND · JUNE 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.94,0:18:36.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Field surgeons used chloroform almost uniformly.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.90,0:18:40.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In the big city hospitals, where there was time and
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.04,0:18:41.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}space, ether was more common.
Dialogue: 2,0:18:34.19,0:18:39.94,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:18:34.19,0:18:39.94,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:18:34.19,0:18:39.94,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:18:34.19,0:18:39.94,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}WARD K · ARMORY SQUARE HOSPITAL, WASHINGTON
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.28,0:18:44.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Some men fought it as it took hold.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.34,0:18:46.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Others feared it would not reach them at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.00,0:18:49.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}One soldier, the National Museum of Civil War
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.66,0:18:52.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Medicine records, was afraid the chloroform would
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.55,0:18:54.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}give out before it got to be his turn.
Dialogue: 2,0:18:42.53,0:18:48.28,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1060 0 l 1060 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:18:42.53,0:18:48.28,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:18:42.53,0:18:48.28,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ENGRAVING · HARPER'S WEEKLY, 1865
Dialogue: 3,0:18:42.53,0:18:48.28,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}HOSPITAL TENTS AND WAGON · PETERSBURG, 1864–65
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.59,0:19:44.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}So when the surgeon reached for the saw, you were
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.25,0:19:45.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}very likely asleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.28,0:19:47.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}What happened next was the second thing the movies
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.00,0:19:48.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}get wrong.
Dialogue: 2,0:19:41.84,0:19:47.59,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1360 0 l 1360 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:19:41.84,0:19:47.59,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:19:41.84,0:19:47.59,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:19:41.84,0:19:47.59,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SURGEONS, SECOND DIVISION, NINTH CORPS · PETERSBURG CAMPAIGN
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.16,0:20:05.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It is easy to call the surgeons butchers.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.90,0:20:07.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Most historians do not.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.44,0:20:08.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Here is why they cut.
Dialogue: 2,0:20:03.41,0:20:09.16,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1210 0 l 1210 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:20:03.41,0:20:09.16,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:20:03.41,0:20:09.16,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:20:03.41,0:20:09.16,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}MEDICAL DIRECTORS, ARMY OF THE CUMBERLAND · JUNE 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.40,0:20:41.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Surgical manuals taught that it should be done
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.88,0:20:43.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}within the first two days.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.28,0:20:44.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The records proved them right.
Dialogue: 2,0:20:39.65,0:20:45.30,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1060 0 l 1060 132 l 0 132{\p0}
