Dialogue: 3,0:20:39.65,0:20:45.30,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SURGEONS OF THE NINTH CORPS · PETERSBURG, 1864
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.49,0:21:28.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And the closer the cut was to the body, the deadlier
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.36,0:21:28.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}it was.
Dialogue: 2,0:21:25.74,0:21:29.15,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:21:25.74,0:21:29.15,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:21:25.74,0:21:29.15,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:21:25.74,0:21:29.15,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SURGEONS AND HOSPITAL STEWARDS IN WASHINGTON
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.63,0:22:07.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Every day there is a fight, he wrote, and every day
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.69,0:22:09.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the hospital is again filled.
Dialogue: 2,0:22:04.88,0:22:09.83,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1060 0 l 1060 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:22:04.88,0:22:09.83,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:22:04.88,0:22:09.83,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ENGRAVING · HARPER'S WEEKLY, 1865
Dialogue: 3,0:22:04.88,0:22:09.83,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FIELD HOSPITAL OF THE NINTH CORPS · PETERSBURG
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.74,0:22:25.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}You have survived the bullet, the field, the cone
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.95,0:22:26.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}and the saw.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.74,0:22:30.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now comes the enemy that nobody in 1862 could see.
Dialogue: 2,0:22:22.99,0:22:28.74,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:22:22.99,0:22:28.74,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:22:22.99,0:22:28.74,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:22:22.99,0:22:28.74,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FIELD HOSPITAL · BRANDY STATION, VA.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.36,0:22:45.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They operated, he said, in old blood-stained coats,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.47,0:22:47.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the veterans of a hundred fights.
Dialogue: 2,0:22:42.61,0:22:47.88,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1124 0 l 1124 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:22:42.61,0:22:47.88,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:22:42.61,0:22:47.88,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:22:42.61,0:22:47.88,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A SURGEON AT HIS TENT · ARMY OF THE POTOMAC, 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.11,0:23:26.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In established cases, the Army admitted, all
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.99,0:23:29.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}remedies were found ineffective.
Dialogue: 2,0:23:24.36,0:23:29.49,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:23:24.36,0:23:29.49,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:23:24.36,0:23:29.49,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:23:24.36,0:23:29.49,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AN EMPTY HOSPITAL WARD · WASHINGTON, D.C.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.65,0:24:03.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And yet, some surgeons were learning by watching.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.67,0:24:06.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A Union surgeon named Middleton Goldsmith began
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.56,0:24:09.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}treating hospital gangrene with bromine, applied
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.52,0:24:10.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}directly to the sore.
Dialogue: 2,0:24:00.90,0:24:06.65,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:24:00.90,0:24:06.65,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:24:00.90,0:24:06.65,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:24:00.90,0:24:06.65,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}OFFICERS' HOSPITAL · NASHVILLE
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.45,0:24:47.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}For the Civil War soldier, it came too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.35,0:24:50.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And in the summer of 1863, the war produced its
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.45,0:24:52.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}largest crowd of wounded yet.
Dialogue: 2,0:24:44.70,0:24:50.45,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:24:44.70,0:24:50.45,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:24:44.70,0:24:50.45,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:24:44.70,0:24:50.45,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE TOWN OF GETTYSBURG · 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.28,0:24:59.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Three days of fighting in southern Pennsylvania,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.39,0:25:00.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}July 1–3, 1863.
Dialogue: 2,0:24:55.53,0:25:01.08,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:24:55.53,0:25:01.08,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:24:55.53,0:25:01.08,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY NATIONAL GUARD VIDEO · DVIDS · 2020
Dialogue: 3,0:24:55.53,0:25:01.08,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}GETTYSBURG BATTLEFIELD TODAY
Dialogue: 0,0:25:26.79,0:25:29.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}I know of no battlefield, Letterman reported, from
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.74,0:25:32.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}which wounded men have been so speedily and so
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.46,0:25:33.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}carefully removed.
Dialogue: 2,0:25:27.04,0:25:32.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1060 0 l 1060 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:25:27.04,0:25:32.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:25:27.04,0:25:32.79,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:25:27.04,0:25:32.79,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AN AMBULANCE TRAIN · WILDERNESS CAMPAIGN, 1864
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.47,0:26:04.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Later, he wrote, I was taken off the table and put
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.32,0:26:07.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}back on my stretcher, which was set down in a wall tent.
Dialogue: 2,0:26:01.72,0:26:07.47,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1038 0 l 1038 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:26:01.72,0:26:07.47,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:26:01.72,0:26:07.47,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:26:01.72,0:26:07.47,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SECOND CORPS HOSPITAL · GETTYSBURG, JULY 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.97,0:26:10.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Fuller had lain in the open before the bearers
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.01,0:26:11.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}reached him.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.80,0:26:14.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}His memoir names that time in four words:
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.51,0:26:16.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}while lying here, entirely helpless.
Dialogue: 2,0:26:08.22,0:26:13.97,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:26:08.22,0:26:13.97,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:26:08.22,0:26:13.97,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:26:08.22,0:26:13.97,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}OPEN GROUND · GETTYSBURG, 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:26:36.26,0:26:37.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}But there was a problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.73,0:26:40.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}By army order, the medical wagons and tents had been
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.93,0:26:43.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}sent to the rear before the battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:43.07,0:26:46.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They could not reach the field in time to protect
Dialogue: 0,0:26:46.08,0:26:49.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the wounded from the drenching rain that fell after it.
Dialogue: 2,0:26:36.51,0:26:42.26,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:26:36.51,0:26:42.26,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:26:36.51,0:26:42.26,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 7 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:26:36.51,0:26:42.26,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}HOSPITAL TENTS · GETTYSBURG, 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.67,0:27:07.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In one corps that kept its wagons, the medical
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.46,0:27:10.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}director reported every man's wounds dressed within
Dialogue: 0,0:27:10.56,0:27:13.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}six hours after the battle ended, and every major
Dialogue: 0,0:27:13.54,0:27:16.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}operation done within twenty-four hours of the wound.
Dialogue: 2,0:27:04.92,0:27:10.67,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1060 0 l 1060 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:27:04.92,0:27:10.67,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:27:04.92,0:27:10.67,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:27:04.92,0:27:10.67,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}OFFICERS AND TENTS · GETTYSBURG CAMPAIGN, 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:27:33.96,0:27:37.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A wounded Confederate officer, held as a prisoner,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:37.41,0:27:38.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}wrote in his diary:
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.71,0:27:42.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}all night long these ambulances move among us, still
Dialogue: 0,0:27:42.30,0:27:43.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}bringing more and more.
Dialogue: 2,0:27:34.21,0:27:39.96,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:27:34.21,0:27:39.96,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:27:34.21,0:27:39.96,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 2 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:27:34.21,0:27:39.96,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE FIELD WHERE PICKETT CHARGED · GETTYSBURG
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.65,0:27:53.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Then the army marched on, and left the town with its
Dialogue: 0,0:27:53.86,0:27:54.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}wounded.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:54.36,0:27:57.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}On a farm about a mile east of Gettysburg, a tent
Dialogue: 0,0:27:57.38,0:27:57.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}city rose:
Dialogue: 0,0:27:58.00,0:27:58.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Camp Letterman.
Dialogue: 2,0:27:50.90,0:27:56.65,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1103 0 l 1103 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:27:50.90,0:27:56.65,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:27:50.90,0:27:56.65,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ENGRAVING · HARPER'S WEEKLY, 1864
Dialogue: 3,0:27:50.90,0:27:56.65,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. SANITARY COMMISSION CAMP · GETTYSBURG, 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.78,0:28:11.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Construction had begun on July 10.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.85,0:28:14.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The Sanitary and Christian Commissions both ran
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.70,0:28:15.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}posts at the camp.
